#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:196
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "All swarm exit criteria have been met or cleanly parked, the final two-table Human-Consumable Swarm Status Report is published, and the Swarm Work Item state is synced."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:43
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Background workers operating in isolated git worktrees, one disjoint slice and one child work item per worker (plus right-scoped non-heavy idle-backlog items in separate worktrees while waiting on single-core compute). Each worker emits live progress and completion blocks and pushes its branch without merging."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:67
#. Diagram label
msgid "Bind or resume swarm epic"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:22
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Binds or cold-resumes any multi-agent swarm on a parent Swarm Work Item (epic or milestone in beans, for example a repository Stability epic, a proof-closure epic, or a literature-audit epic) carrying measurable exit criteria (EC-1..EC-k), structured child queues (completed, active, queued, idle-backlog), and a live Cold-Start Handover Runbook, then dispatches isolated-worktree workers under a per-swarm spawn gate and supervises them through Process_SwarmMonitorSweep until the epic drains or halts."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:189
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Cancel any remaining wakeup or periodic report timer and run Process_BeanClose on the parent Swarm Work Item: complete and archive once EC-1..EC-k are satisfied, or record explicit blockers and cold-takeover dispatch lines in beans and hand back cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:176
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Claim the next unblocked child work items in the shared beans store (pushing updated queue and handover state to the branch store), dispatch fresh isolated-worktree workers into freed slots with the mandatory role-specific Process & Skill Launch Block and progress contract, and re-arm the 2-to-4-minute one-shot fallback timer before ending the turn."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:116
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Claim the parent Swarm Work Item and initial worker sub-beans in the shared beans store through Process_BeanOpen and push state to the branch store so sibling sessions see every active claim and handover header."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:188
#. Diagram label
msgid "Close or park swarm epic"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:31
#. Diagram label
msgid "Coordinator"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:96
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Coordinator posts the full context, exit criteria, worker count, model tiers, relative token cost, reporting mode (on-demand vs periodic), options, and recommendation in chat, followed immediately by a tappable card; the owner approves or declines."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:95
#. Diagram label
msgid "Decide swarm card"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:80
#. Diagram label
msgid "Decompose disjoint sub-beans"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:123
#. Diagram label
msgid "Dispatch workers with skill brief"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:220
#. Diagram label
msgid "Drained"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:131
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Each worker executes its claimed disjoint slice in its worktree (or advances a right-scoped non-heavy idle-backlog item in a separate worktree while waiting on single-core compute, never checking out mid-build), emits live progress blocks, runs verification, pushes its branch and PR, and emits DONE without merging."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:130
#. Diagram label
msgid "Execute slice or idle backlog"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:32
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Finds, cold-resumes, or idempotently initializes the parent Swarm Work Item (acceptance criteria EC-1..EC-k, child queues, and handover runbook), decomposes disjoint sub-beans and non-heavy idle-backlog items, opens the swarm epic via Process_BeanOpen, and dispatches isolated-worktree workers with the mandatory fresh-context Process & Skill Launch Block, progress contract, and wakeup schedule."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:28
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Grants or declines per-swarm spawn permission on a tappable decision card after reading worker count, model tiers, relative token cost, and status reporting preference (on-demand vs periodic) in chat, unless a bounded swarm-spawn waiver already covers the scope."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:154
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Hand the verified six-line merge request (or ready-to-merge / needs-repin label) to the active merge steward for batch approval and merge-train landing; neither workers nor monitor self-merge outside the merge-steward lane."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:161
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Join after optional merge-steward handoff before evaluating remaining worker slots, exit criteria EC-1..EC-k, and queued beans."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:56
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge steward"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:205
#. Diagram label
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:115
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the swarm epic"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:27
#. Diagram label
msgid "Owner"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:63
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Parallel workstreams are requested for a goal epic, or a successor coordinator/merge-steward takes over cold after a session stall exceeding the liveness window."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:68
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Query beans for an active parent Swarm Work Item (epic or milestone, parameterized by --epic-id or --swarm-title; check before creating). On cold takeover after a stall, read its Cold-Start Handover Runbook first; otherwise define measurable exit criteria (EC-1..EC-k), structured child queues (completed, active, queued, idle-backlog), and user-selected status cadence (on-demand vs periodic)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:153
#. Diagram label
msgid "Queue PR in merge watch"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Receives six-line merge requests for independently verified pull requests and routes them through the merge train or direct merge guard under the owner's batch approval, keeping merge-wave state reflected in the shared work plan."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:175
#. Diagram label
msgid "Refill slots and re-arm timer"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:139
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Run Process_SwarmMonitorSweep on reactive wakeups, routine check-in ticks, or on-demand status requests: inspect worker progress, queues, and compressed/swap memory, triage leaks or stalls, assign non-heavy idle-backlog items to compute-bound workers, push a fresh Cold-Start Handover Runbook to beans, and emit the two-table status report when due."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:110
#. Diagram label
msgid "Run serially"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs Process_SwarmMonitorSweep on reactive worker events, routine check-in ticks, or on-demand status requests to check progress and compressed/swap headroom, assign idle-on-compute backlog, refresh and push the Swarm Work Item's Cold-Start Handover Runbook, and publish anti-shorthand status tables; then hands verified PRs to the merge steward, refills freed slots, and closes via Process_BeanClose when drained."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:167
#. Diagram label
msgid "Slots active or refillable?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:102
#. Diagram label
msgid "Spawn approved?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:124
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Spawned siblings start with a blank context: inject the mandatory role-specific Process & Skill Launch Block into every worker prompt (for a Merge Steward: repo local skills, merge-manager-watcher, merge-queue / Process_MergeTrain + merge-overlap + Process_MergeRefusal, merge-to-main + Task_LocalGates + verify-merge-replay, merge-conflict-patterns, and beans show <epic-id>; for any Task Sibling: target repo .claude/skills/local/*.md first, continual-progress, idle-backlog without passive sleep timers or mid-build git checkout, merge-request / merge-queue never-self-merge 6-line handoff, interaction-modality / hand-back-to-discussion, one-voice-style-guide, and repo fences), plus the verbatim PROGRESS contract; arm the 2-to-4-minute fallback timer."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:195
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swarm closed"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:111
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Swarm declined or unjustified; work proceeds sequentially one child work item at a time."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:19
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swarm dispatch and monitor"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:46
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swarm monitor"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:62
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swarm start or takeover"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:87
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swarm-spawn waived?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:138
#. Diagram label
msgid "Sweep, triage and sync handover"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:145
#. Diagram label
msgid "Verified PR ready?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Verify that a swarm is justified over serial execution (swarm-management), partition the goal into child work items with disjoint writable paths, explicit Done-when criteria, and non-compute-heavy idle-backlog items, and size worker count, model tiers (cost-aware routing), and host concurrency bounds."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:200
#. Diagram label
msgid "Work plan (beans)"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:42
#. Diagram label
msgid "Worker agents"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:206
#. Diagram label
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:146
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when a completed worker branch passes independent parent verification (typecheck, tests, and applicable gates) and is ready for merge-steward intake. No when workers are still running or blocked."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:88
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when an active owner confirmation waiver explicitly covers swarm-spawn up to this worker count and model tier, quoted in the turn report. No otherwise: ask first, per swarm."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:103
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes when the owner approves the swarm card. No when declined: fall back to sequential execution."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/swarm-dispatch-and-monitor.bpmn:168
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Yes while workers remain live or unclaimed, unblocked child items remain before exit criteria EC-1..EC-k are all met, with healthy host headroom and no Andon halt. Drained when all EC-1..EC-k gates pass, items are parked on an owner decision card, or the Andon cord halts execution."
msgstr ""
